@Plumy.Api_HostAddress = https://localhost:7062

### Create a client company (201 + Location header)
# @name create
POST {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme S.L.",
  "taxId": "b-1234567.4"
}

### Get it back using the Id from the previous response
GET {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies/{{create.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json

### Same tax ID again → 409 Conflict
POST {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Duplicate S.L.",
  "taxId": "B12345674"
}

### Invalid tax ID → 400 ProblemDetails
POST {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad S.L.",
  "taxId": "B12345670"
}

### Unknown Id → 404
GET {{Plumy.Api_HostAddress}}/api/client-companies/{{$random.uuid}}
Accept: application/json
